# Asset integrity
- Check `Panther_Passage_Visual_Assets/ASSET_MANIFEST.json` and real file paths before referencing an asset. Existing starter illustrations are **provisional**, not approved originals.
- Preserve approved Panther Passage branding precisely; never regenerate or pretend official university insignia/campus photography are authentic. Label stylized campus interpretations.
- Approved welcome visuals take priority over generating new scenery; preserve visible walkways, architecture and reduced greenery.
- Use `@phosphor-icons/react` for functional icons, not exported raster icon sheets. Document icon names and weights in `ICON_SYSTEM.md` when present.
- Custom journey medallions, chapter emblems, reward crests and finale art belong to the branded asset library. Do not replace them with generic Phosphor icons as a final solution.
- Use optimized responsive formats and appropriate `alt` text (empty alt for purely decorative imagery). Provide fixed aspect/size to minimize layout shifts and lazy load nonessential illustrations.
- Never use a non-existent path as though it works. If artwork is missing, implement an accessible named fallback and record the missing asset in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_AUDIT.md`.
- Environment backgrounds must not contain baked-in labels, buttons, milestones or interactive controls unless explicitly a noninteractive preview.
